   "Statement": "<b>Occupation</b><br>Washington State Industrial Appeals Judge and Pierce County District Court Judge Pro Tem. Former Deputy Prosecuting Attorney.</p><p style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 0px;\"><br><b>Education</b><br>University of Washington School of Law, J.D.<br><br><b>Statement</b><br>Neil Horibe has earned the trust of the Pierce County legal community with the <em>highest</em> rating from the Tacoma-Pierce County Bar Association: \"Exceptionally Well Qualified.\" He is endorsed by Court of Appeals Judges and a majority of Superior and District Court Judges, including retiring incumbent Judge Lloyd Oaks.</p><p></p><p style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 0px;\">The grandchild of Japanese Americans interned by the United States during World War II, he believes every person deserves dignity, a fair and unbiased hearing, and the rights guaranteed by the law. As a Deputy Prosecutor, he tried felony and misdemeanor cases including DUI, sexual assault, and murder.</p><p></p><p style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 0px;\">Bringing judicial experience as a Washington State Industrial Appeals Judge and Pierce County District Court Judge Pro Tem, he is ready to serve on day one. \"<em>I promise to listen carefully, rule based on the law and facts, and treat every person with dignity and respect. I humbly ask for your vote.</em>\"</p><p> </p><p style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 0px;\">",
